    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4cf873fd-d90d-5a95-bd0c-02f2d1d89f52",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=-3 \\\\ -6x-4y &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\nII. The system is consistent dependent\nIII. The system is inconsistent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=1,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a0f9464b-6da9-56a2-8807-6e99ed009c4a",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
